      ":question/math-academy-id": "e-4294",
      ":question/problem": "Let $\\mathbf{a}={\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}1 \\\\ - 5\\end{array} \\right]},$ $\\mathbf{b}={\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}2 \\\\ 4\\end{array} \\right]},$ and $\\mathbf{c}={\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}- 3 \\\\ 7\\end{array} \\right]}.$ Find $2\\mathbf{a}-(\\mathbf{b}-5\\mathbf{c})$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To compute the result, we just need to perform the required operations with each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2a - (b - 5c) &= 2 \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix} - (\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} - 5 \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -10\\end{bmatrix} - (\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} - \\begin{bmatrix}-15 \\\\ 35\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -10\\end{bmatrix} - \\begin{bmatrix}17 \\\\ -31\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}-15 \\\\ 21\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
