        ":question/id": "2a5c3b4f-534d-508b-a057-66300261cf45",
        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-18041",
        ":question/problem": "Let $a = \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$, $b = \\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ and $c = \\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}$. Find $a - (2b + 5c)$."
