        ":question/id": "aad6285a-b3b6-504e-bdb1-d51f41010e44",
        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-70414",
        ":question/problem": "Let $a=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$, $b=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}$ and $c=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.$ Find $a+(2b-2c).$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "To compute the result, we just need to perform the required operations with each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a+(2b-2c) & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+(2\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}-2\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+(\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"
      },
