        ":question/id": "5042d60d-1d74-5a97-ae4c-6f45b8b23e98",
        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-318151",
        ":question/problem": "Let $a=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$, $b=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}$ and $c=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}.$ Find $2b+(-3a+c).$\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"1\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"25\">$2b+(-3a+c)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"2\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">{{field-1}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"2\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"2\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">{{field-2}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"2\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>",
        ":question/worked-solution": "To compute the result, we just need to perform the required operations with each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2b+(-3a+c) & =2\\,\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}+(-3\\,\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}+(\\begin{bmatrix}12 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}16 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"
      },
