        ":question/id": "df07f0e4-b8c0-55c8-a0ad-afd25f375b3a",
        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-318154",
        ":question/problem": "Let $a=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$, $b=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}$ and $c=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}.$ Find $\\,4a-(3b-2c).$\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"1\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"25\">$4a-(3b-2c)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"2\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">{{field-1}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"2\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"2\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">{{field-2}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"2\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>",
        ":question/worked-solution": "To compute the result, we just need to perform the required operations with each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4a-(3b-2c) & =4\\,\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}-(3\\,\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}-2\\,\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-20 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix}-(\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-20 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -24\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-28 \\\\ 36\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
      }
